class.description:
Child [CanvasItem] nodes of a [CanvasGroup] are drawn as a single object. It allows to e.g. draw overlapping translucent 2D nodes without causing the overlapping sections to be more opaque than intended (set the [member CanvasItem.self_modulate] property on the [CanvasGroup] to achieve this effect).
[b]Note:[/b] The [CanvasGroup] draws its composited children as the current CanvasItem [code]TEXTURE[/code]. Assigning a [Material] to the [CanvasGroup] replaces the default CanvasItem shader. To duplicate the default behavior in a custom [Shader], use the following:
[codeblock]
shader_type canvas_item;
render_mode unshaded;

void fragment() {
}
[/codeblock]
The CanvasGroup compositing source uses associated alpha, so its RGB values are already multiplied by alpha. CanvasGroup output is blended back using premultiplied alpha blending.
[b]Note:[/b] Drawing commands issued by the [CanvasGroup] owner itself are not supported. Place drawable content in child [CanvasItem] nodes, and use a [ShaderMaterial] on the [CanvasGroup] to customize how the composited children texture is drawn.
[b]Note:[/b] When using a RenderingDevice-based renderer, [CanvasGroup] nodes can be nested. Nested [CanvasGroup] nodes are rendered from the innermost group outward, similar to nested layer groups in image editing applications. This is not supported by the Compatibility renderer.
[b]Note:[/b] Since [CanvasGroup] and [member CanvasItem.clip_children] both utilize offscreen buffers, children of a [CanvasGroup] who have their [member CanvasItem.clip_children] set to anything other than [constant CanvasItem.CLIP_CHILDREN_DISABLED] will not function correctly.
